diff --git a/docs/overview.md b/docs/overview.md
index 15d5d1cb..9681c4d3 100644
--- a/docs/overview.md
+++ b/docs/overview.md
@@ -747,6 +747,7 @@ User-facing modules each get one `lym <module>` namespace:
   uncommitted content in the task worktree itself keeps fabric's refusal, and neither is ever `--force`.
   A fresh pair's records branch starts without its parent's `_lym/shed/` run records, which fabric's `add` drops in the pair's first records commit, so a child never sees prime's batten records or any other run's.
   `Worktree-Create` and `Worktree-Teardown` wait for a prime lock another run holds, polling every 2 s for up to 10 min, and halt `blocked` only once that wait runs out.
+  `Worktree-Create` holds it only while fabric's `add` reads the fork point and writes the hub's worktree registry, never over the board claim, the config reconcile or the pair's push, and over origin's probes only for the time they still need once the pre-flight reads are done, so runs started together create their pairs side by side.
   `step` drives exactly one producer forward from the run's persisted current producer, seeding a fresh run first when none is persisted yet.
   `lym loom step` is the single-producer primitive of the same shape over a run that is already seeded.
   `run` and `step` carry `--driver` (batten's own, `go`-only: batten has no bootstrap verb, so `llm` is refused by name) and `--child-driver` (the driver the task worktree's own inner run uses, `llm` or `go`; unset, `shed.yaml`'s `driver_kind`, `go` by default); `--driver` is recorded into the run's write-once seed at first seeding and `--child-driver` only when typed, and an explicitly typed flag that disagrees with an already-seeded run is refused rather than silently dropped.
